# DocForge configuration — copy to `.env` and edit. (`.env` is gitignored; never commit secrets.)
# Precedence for every setting: an explicit CLI flag > this .env / environment > the built-in default.
# Any line you leave out just falls back to the default (local Docker Qdrant + ./docforge.db).

# Where the SQLite manifest (page hashes, per knowledge base) lives.
# Default: docforge.db in the current directory. Point it anywhere you like.
# DOCFORGE_DB=SqlDB/docforge.db

# --- Vector store: choose ONE of the two below (or neither = local Docker Qdrant) ---

# A) Remote / Qdrant Cloud (or any Qdrant server). Include the port (:6333).
# QDRANT_URL=https://YOUR-CLUSTER.aws.cloud.qdrant.io:6333
# QDRANT_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# B) Embedded Qdrant — no Docker, vectors stored in this local folder (like SQLite).
#    (Takes precedence over QDRANT_URL if both are set.)
# QDRANT_PATH=./vectors

# fastembed model name for embeddings. Must stay the same across syncs of the same
# knowledge base -- switching models changes the vector dimension.
# Default: BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5
# DOCFORGE_EMBED_MODEL=BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5

# --- docforge-mcp (the MCP server) ---

# Default transport if --transport isn't passed: stdio, http, or both.
# DOCFORGE_MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio

# A stable auth token for the http side, so it doesn't regenerate (and need re-pasting into
# your client config) on every restart. Without this, a fresh token is generated and printed
# each time you run `docforge-mcp --transport http`.
# DOCFORGE_MCP_TOKEN=your-own-generated-token
